+$s_1$ in the first !!{element}.  Whatever $s_1(1)$ is, we defined
+
+$\overline{s}(1)$ to be the opposite.  It can't be the second
+
+sequence in the list, because $\overline{s}$ differs from $s_2$ in the second
+
